      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "mkinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-21T09:39:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): read a drafted side as a wall, not as a modelled chamfer\n\nA no-pick 2D chamfer refused a plate with one drafted side (#2894's\npartly bevelled law): a draft over about 3 degrees puts the top edge more\nthan 0.05 mm off the wall at the corner depth, which read as a bevel.\n\nThe ride now takes a third section, half way down. A piece off its wall\nis a drafted wall when it stands at most tan(15 deg) of the depth off\nthe wall and the half-depth section stands half that off it: one\nstraight face at a draft's slope. A loop with drafted pieces and no\nbevelled one rides its wall with the sharp loops. The #2887 refusal\nholds for a modelled bevel, a small one (half-depth section on the\nwall) and a 45 degree one deeper than the ride.\n\nFixes #2929\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
